<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK NAFTA POSTS SKK 220.2 MLN H1 1997 NET.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK NAFTA POSTS SKK 220.2 MLN H1 1997 NET.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six-month period</p>
<p>ending June 30, 1997: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> After-tax profit		220.227		 409.104</p>
<p> Operating revenues	  1,556.698	     1,961.295</p>
<p> Operating costs	     1,173.408	     1,346.376</p>
<p> Operating profit		383.290		 614.919</p>
<p>Revenues from</p>
<p>  financial operations	  20.638		  54.645</p>
<p>Results from</p>
<p>  financial operations	 -34.960		 -23.224</p>
<p> Financial costs		  55.598		  77.869</p>
<p> Reserves			   11.899		   0.000</p>
<p> Total loans		     478.593		 538.398</p>
<p>  Long-term loans		379.441		 538.398</p>
<p>  Short-term loans		99.152		   0.000</p>
<p> Basic capital		 3,230.960	     3,230.960</p>
<p> Total assets		  8.147.902	     7,206.745</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Nafta a.s. Gbely. The company</p>
<p>has a dominant position on the Slovak natural gas and oil</p>
<p>exploration markets as well as underground gas storage. Nafta's</p>
<p>major shareholders include Druha Obchodna a.s. (45.9 percent),</p>
<p>Chase Nominees Ltd London (7.5 percent), VUB Bank (6.9 percent)</p>
<p>and Creditanstalt Bankverein Wien (5.8 percent).</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
